Subject: amd64/isel: mask constant shift counts
Origin: Filnix
Upstream-Status: Not submitted
Base: c0818978acec60ebb6167fade60fb7012cbf20ca

The IL takes shift counts modulo the width of the result, and the cpu
masks the count to 5 or 6 bits, but a constant count was emitted as is.
GNU as rejects an immediate count that does not fit in 8 bits:

	%x =l shl %a, 300   # shlq $300, %rax

Mask constant counts to 6 bits; the cpu still masks word shifts to 5.
Regression: filnix nanofil/tests/gen.py shifts by unmasked constants.

diff --git a/amd64/isel.c b/amd64/isel.c
index 0f514de..0386f50 100644
--- a/amd64/isel.c
+++ b/amd64/isel.c
@@ -307,8 +307,16 @@ sel(Ins i, Num *tn, Fn *fn)
 	case Oshr:
 	case Oshl:
 		r0 = i.arg[1];
-		if (rtype(r0) == RCon)
+		if (rtype(r0) == RCon) {
+			/* the assembler wants an 8-bit
+			 * count, the cpu masks it anyway
+			 */
+			if (fn->con[r0.val].type == CBits) {
+				sh = fn->con[r0.val].bits.i & 63;
+				i.arg[1] = getcon(sh, fn);
+			}
 			goto Emit;
+		}
 		if (fn->tmp[r0.val].slot != -1)
 			err("unlikely argument %%%s in %s",
 				fn->tmp[r0.val].name, optab[i.op].name);
